================================================================================
SCOPE, AND TERMS THAT APPLY TO THINGS THIS SOFTWARE TOUCHES
================================================================================

The MIT licence above covers the MyGardenBird pipeline SOURCE CODE only. Three
other sets of terms apply to material the pipeline produces or depends on, and
none of them is altered by the licence above.

THE DATASET IS NOT MIT LICENSED.

  The MyGardenBird dataset -- the audio clips and the metadata tables -- is
  released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, reflecting the most restrictive upstream
  terms among the Xeno-canto recordings it derives from. See
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20306876

  Attribution is due to the individual Xeno-canto recordists, not only to the
  dataset authors; recordings.csv carries the recordist and xc_url fields for
  every source recording.

SOURCE RECORDINGS CARRY THEIR OWN LICENCES.

  Clips are derived works of Xeno-canto recordings, each under its own
  Creative Commons licence. Recordings licensed CC BY-NC-ND are excluded from
  the dataset, because segmenting a recording produces a derivative work that
  the NoDerivatives term does not permit to be distributed. If you use this
  pipeline to build your own corpus, that exclusion is yours to enforce: see
  the --no-skip-nd flag on Stages 2 and 2a, which disables it.

BIRDNET MODEL WEIGHTS ARE NON-COMMERCIAL.

  Stage 7 evaluates clips with BirdNET. The BirdNET-Analyzer source code is
  MIT licensed, but the model weights it loads -- from the installed
  birdnet_analyzer package, not from this repository -- are released by the
  Cornell Lab of Ornithology under a non-commercial Creative Commons licence.
  Running Stage 7 in a commercial setting therefore needs permission from
  Cornell, regardless of this MIT licence. Nothing here embeds or
  redistributes those weights.
